# What the image build never needs. The Dockerfile copies pyproject.toml, README.md and
# nanomuse_cloud/ only, but without this file the whole directory, the database under
# data/ and .env included, is sent to the Docker daemon as the build context. A pattern
# without `**/` matches at the root only (Go's filepath.Match, not gitignore), so the caches
# under nanomuse_cloud/ need the prefix or they ride along in the COPY.
.env
.env.*
*.env
data/
deploy/
tests/
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/*.egg-info
